 "notes": "INTERPRETER LIMITATION: an SG-to-SG rule written as a separate aws_security_group_rule / aws_vpc_security_group_ingress_rule references two SGs (target + source), but a ref leaf can only require one target, and security_group_id/source_security_group_id are unknown at plan. So for the separate-rule shape each pairing is checked as two halves: the target SG has an SG-sourced (no CIDR) ingress rule on the port, and the source SG is referenced by an SG-sourced rule on that port. A candidate that swaps sources between targets on the same port (e.g. port 22) could pass. The inline-ingress shape is checked precisely. Multi-AZ placement of the two RDS subnets is not checked (availability_zone is not stated literally in the prompt and may be computed)."
